<title>USA: Old Bridge, N.J., weighs tax lien deal -- paper.</title>
<headline>Old Bridge, N.J., weighs tax lien deal -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Officials in Old Bridge, N.J., are at odds over whether to appropriate $500,000 to purchase property tax liens, the Star Ledger reported Thursday.</p>
<p>Mayor Barbara Cannon proposed the plan, which would raise money to pay for sick and vacation days accumulated by retiring town employees.</p>
<p>Councilman Edward Testino, however, has questioned the prudence of a tax lien deal, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>--Steven Dickson, 212-859-1652</p>
